---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---
<section class="brands-how">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead eyebrow="how it works" html="How we work with brands" />
    <div class="brands-narrow">
      <p class="brands-lead">A few things to know upfront, so there are no surprises later.</p>
      <p>Sunday is free. Always has been, always will be. The regular Sunday reading is open to everyone at no charge. If a partnership involves an optional add-on — a book signing, a workshop, a curated reading at a special venue — that smaller event might be paid for the people who want to attend it. The regular Sunday on the same day still runs, still free, still open.</p>
      <p>WhatsApp groups are mostly quiet. If we're working with a brand on something useful — a free audiobook trial, a discount at a bookshop we're reading at, an event we want people to know about — we'll mention it once in the groups. We don't run unrelated promotions and we don't sell access to the lists.</p>
      <p>The reader's data isn't for sale. We share aggregate audience information with potential partners — who reads, where they live, what they're into — but never individual contact details, names, or attendance records.</p>
      <p>Sundays look the same for everyone. No paid tier, no premium seating, no priority access. A regular Sunday and a partner Sunday read the same to the reader. That's how we keep it honest.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
